{"type":"message","id":"c9b6adea","parentId":"854fd4f6","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:42:30.758Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"安装成功了。不过接下来需要让 OpenClaw 识别这个技能。我需要检查 OpenClaw 的配置，看看 skills 的配置方式。\n\n通常，技能安装在 ~/.openclaw/skills/ 目录下会被自动发现，但有时需要在 openclaw.json 中配置。让我检查一下当前的 skills 配置。","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"安装成功！让我验证一下安装内容并检查"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b4117c805aa44d349d10a948","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /home/node/.openclaw/skills/doc-summarize-pro/","timeout":5},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"ls -la /home/node/.openclaw/skills/doc-summarize-pro/\", \"timeout\": 5}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7c02a2e7cea649608cfa48de","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /home/node/.openclaw/skills/doc-summarize-pro/SKILL.md | head -60","timeout":5},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"cat /home/node/.openclaw/skills/doc-summarize-pro/SKILL.md | head -60\", \"timeout\": 5}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779511309350,"responseId":"e2747ad4c22249deb66c1a3c9d672415"}}
{"type":"message","id":"7fa73e6b","parentId":"c9b6adea","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:42:30.825Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b4117c805aa44d349d10a948","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"total 28\ndrwxr-xr-x  4 node node 4096 May 23 04:41 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 16 node node 4096 May 23 04:41 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 node node 4096 May 23 04:41 .clawhub\n-rw-r--r--  1 node node 3375 May 23 04:41 SKILL.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 node node  136 May 23 04:41 _meta.json\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 node node 4096 May 23 04:41 scripts\n-rw-r--r--  1 node node 1065 May 23 04:41 tips.md"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":28,"aggregated":"total 28\ndrwxr-xr-x  4 node node 4096 May 23 04:41 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 16 node node 4096 May 23 04:41 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 node node 4096 May 23 04:41 .clawhub\n-rw-r--r--  1 node node 3375 May 23 04:41 SKILL.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 node node  136 May 23 04:41 _meta.json\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 node node 4096 May 23 04:41 scripts\n-rw-r--r--  1 node node 1065 May 23 04:41 tips.md","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-wxlee"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779511350820}}
{"type":"message","id":"4a0d65d5","parentId":"7fa73e6b","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:42:30.830Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_7c02a2e7cea649608cfa48de","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nversion: \"3.0.0\"\nname: doc-summarize-pro\ndescription: \"Enhanced document summarizer. Smart summary, bullet extraction, executive summary, chapter breakdown, multi-doc comparison, translate+summarize.\"\nauthor: BytesAgain\nhomepage: https://bytesagain.com\nsource: https://github.com/bytesagain/ai-skills\n---\n\n# 📝 Doc Summarize Pro — Document Analysis Toolkit\n\n> Pure-bash document summarizer: extract summaries, keywords, outlines, stats, and more — no external dependencies.\n\n## Commands\n\n### `summarize <file>`\n\nGenerate a document summary by extracting key sentences from each paragraph (first and last sentences, plus topic sentences).\n\n### `keywords <file>`\n\nExtract keywords via word-frequency analysis. Filters common stop-words and ranks by occurrence count.\n\n### `outline <file>`\n\nExtract document structure and outline by detecting heading lines (Markdown `#` headers, ALL-CAPS lines, numbered sections).\n\n### `stats <file>`\n\nDocument statistics: word count, character count, paragraph count, sentence count, unique words, and estimated reading time.\n\n### `compare <file1> <file2>`\n\nCompare two documents side-by-side: word count difference, shared keywords, and unique keywords per file.\n\n### `batch <dir>`\n\nBatch-summarize all text files in a directory. Processes `.txt`, `.md`, `.rst`, `.log` files and outputs a summary for each.\n\n### `export <file> <format>`\n\nExport a file's summary in a specified format. Supported formats: `md` (Markdown), `txt` (plain text), `json`.\n\n### `history`\n\nDisplay processing history — shows all previously run commands with timestamps.\n\n### `config`\n\nView or update configuration. Settings: `summary_sentences` (sentences per paragraph in summary), `keyword_count` (max keywords to display).\n\n### `help`\n\nShow usage information and available commands.\n\n### `version`\n\nPrint the current version number.\n\n## Examples"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":30,"aggregated":"---\nversion: \"3.0.0\"\nname: doc-summarize-pro\ndescription: \"Enhanced document summarizer. Smart summary, bullet extraction, executive summary, chapter breakdown, multi-doc comparison, translate+summarize.\"\nauthor: BytesAgain\nhomepage: https://bytesagain.com\nsource: https://github.com/bytesagain/ai-skills\n---\n\n# 📝 Doc Summarize Pro — Document Analysis Toolkit\n\n> Pure-bash document summarizer: extract summaries, keywords, outlines, stats, and more — no external dependencies.\n\n## Commands\n\n### `summarize <file>`\n\nGenerate a document summary by extracting key sentences from each paragraph (first and last sentences, plus topic sentences).\n\n### `keywords <file>`\n\nExtract keywords via word-frequency analysis. Filters common stop-words and ranks by occurrence count.\n\n### `outline <file>`\n\nExtract document structure and outline by detecting heading lines (Markdown `#` headers, ALL-CAPS lines, numbered sections).\n\n### `stats <file>`\n\nDocument statistics: word count, character count, paragraph count, sentence count, unique words, and estimated reading time.\n\n### `compare <file1> <file2>`\n\nCompare two documents side-by-side: word count difference, shared keywords, and unique keywords per file.\n\n### `batch <dir>`\n\nBatch-summarize all text files in a directory. Processes `.txt`, `.md`, `.rst`, `.log` files and outputs a summary for each.\n\n### `export <file> <format>`\n\nExport a file's summary in a specified format. Supported formats: `md` (Markdown), `txt` (plain text), `json`.\n\n### `history`\n\nDisplay processing history — shows all previously run commands with timestamps.\n\n### `config`\n\nView or update configuration. Settings: `summary_sentences` (sentences per paragraph in summary), `keyword_count` (max keywords to display).\n\n### `help`\n\nShow usage information and available commands.\n\n### `version`\n\nPrint the current version number.\n\n## Examples","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-wxlee"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779511350820}}
