y to \"allowlist\" after confirming omitted  │\n│    bundled providers are intentionally blocked.                      │\n\n\nProcess exited with signal SIGTERM."}],"details":{"status":"failed","sessionId":"nimble-nexus","aggregated":"Config valid: ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json\n---\n▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄\n██░▄▄▄░██░▄▄░██░▄▄▄██░▀██░██░▄▄▀██░████░▄▄▀██░███░██\n██░███░██░▀▀░██░▄▄▄██░█░█░██░█████░████░▀▀░██░█░█░██\n██░▀▀▀░██░█████░▀▀▀██░██▄░██░▀▀▄██░▀▀░█░██░██▄▀▄▀▄██\n▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀\n                       OPENCLAW                       \n \n┌  OpenClaw doctor\n│\n◇  Startup optimization ────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│                                                                       │\n│  - NODE_COMPILE_CACHE is not set; repeated CLI runs can be slower on  │\n│    small hosts (Pi/VM).                                               │\n│  - OPENCLAW_NO_RESPAWN is not set to 1; set it when you want routine  │\n│    gateway restarts to stay in-process instead of handing off to a    │\n│    managed supervisor.                                                │\n│  - Suggested env for low-power hosts:                                 │\n│    export NODE_COMPILE_CACHE=/var/tmp/openclaw-compile-cache          │\n│    mkdir -p /var/tmp/openclaw-compile-cache                           │\n│    export OPENCLAW_NO_RESPAWN=1                                       │\n│                                                                       │\n├───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n│\n◇  Doctor warnings ────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│                                                                      │\n│  - plugins.allow is restrictive, but bundled provider discovery is   │\n│    still in legacy compatibility mode. Bundled provider plugins can  │\n│    still appear in runtime provider inventories; set                 │\n│    plugins.bundle