{"type":"message","id":"de33f3a4","parentId":"9e26e15a","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:50:20.343Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I restored the config. Now I see the issue - the skill entry format for doc-summarize-pro might not accept \"from\" field. Let me look at how existing skills are configured to understand the correct format. Let me check the docs or search for the schema.\n\nActually, looking at the existing entries, they all just have `{\"enabled\": false}` without any `from` field. Maybe for locally installed skills, the skill just needs to be in the skills directory and the entry in openclaw.json only needs `enabled: true`. Let me check the documentation.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9e04d41079b5400d9afa3702","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/app/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md","limit":50,"offset":1},"partialArgs":"{\"path\": \"/app/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md\", \"limit\": 50, \"offset\": 1}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8ac1e81274e842ce8c74220d","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"skills\" /app/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md | head -30","timeout":5},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"grep -n \\\"skills\\\" /app/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md | head -30\", \"timeout\": 5}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779511812945,"responseId":"d4b95a9bbb0b4bc0aac97acdc2cc073c"}}
{"type":"message","id":"a854f04d","parentId":"de33f3a4","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:50:20.389Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_9e04d41079b5400d9afa3702","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nsummary: \"Gateway config reference for core OpenClaw keys, defaults, and links to dedicated subsystem references\"\ntitle: \"Configuration reference\"\nread_when:\n  - You need exact field-level config semantics or defaults\n  - You are validating channel, model, gateway, or tool config blocks\n---\n\nCore config reference for `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`. For a task-oriented overview, see [Configuration](/gateway/configuration).\n\nCovers the main OpenClaw config surfaces and links out when a subsystem has its own deeper reference. Channel- and plugin-owned command catalogs and deep memory/QMD knobs live on their own pages rather than on this one.\n\nCode truth:\n\n- `openclaw config schema` prints the live JSON Schema used for validation and Control UI, with bundled/plugin/channel metadata merged in when available\n- `config.schema.lookup` returns one path-scoped schema node for drill-down tooling\n- `pnpm config:docs:check` / `pnpm config:docs:gen` validate the config-doc baseline hash against the current schema surface\n\nAgent lookup path: use the `gateway` tool action `config.schema.lookup` for\nexact field-level docs and constraints before edits. Use\n[Configuration](/gateway/configuration) for task-oriented guidance and this page\nfor the broader field map, defaults, and links to subsystem references.\n\nDedicated deep references:\n\n- [Memory configuration reference](/reference/memory-config) for `agents.defaults.memorySearch.*`, `memory.qmd.*`, `memory.citations`, and dreaming config under `plugins.entries.memory-core.config.dreaming`\n- [Slash commands](/tools/slash-commands) for the current built-in + bundled command catalog\n- owning channel/plugin pages for channel-specific command surfaces\n\nConfig format is **JSON5** (comments + trailing commas allowed). All fields are optional - OpenClaw uses safe defaults when omitted.\n\n---\n\n## Channels\n\nPer-channel config keys moved to a dedicated page - see\n[Configuration - channels](/gateway/config-channels) for `channels.*`,\nincluding Slack, Discord, Telegram, WhatsApp, Matrix, iMessage, and other\nbundled channels (auth, access control, multi-account, mention gating).\n\n## Agent defaults, multi-agent, sessions, and messages\n\nMoved to a dedicated page - see\n[Configuration - agents](/gateway/config-agents) for:\n\n- `agents.defaults.*` (workspace, model, thinking, heartbeat, memory, media, skills, sandbox)\n- `multiAgent.*` (multi-agent routing and bindings)\n- `session.*` (session lifecycle, compaction, pruning)\n- `messages.*` (message delivery, TTS, markdown rendering)\n- `talk.*` (Talk mode)\n\n[1344 more lines in file. Use offset=51 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779511820386}}
{"type":"message","id":"cc9d516f","parentId":"a854f04d","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:50:20.392Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8ac1e81274e842ce8c74220d","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"46:- `agents.defaults.*` (workspace, model, thinking, heartbeat, memory, media, skills, sandbox)\n152:  skills: {\n155:      extraDirs: [\"~/Projects/agent-scripts/skills\"],\n156:      allowSymlinkTargets: [\"~/Projects/manager/skills\"],\n175:- `allowBundled`: optional allowlist for bundled skills only (managed/workspace skills unaffected).\n184:  clients to install private zip archives staged through `skills.upload.*`\n188:- `entries.<skillKey>.apiKey`: convenience for skills declaring a primary env var (plaintext string or SecretRef object)."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":20,"aggregated":"46:- `agents.defaults.*` (workspace, model, thinking, heartbeat, memory, media, skills, sandbox)\n152:  skills: {\n155:      extraDirs: [\"~/Projects/agent-scripts/skills\"],\n156:      allowSymlinkTargets: [\"~/Projects/manager/skills\"],\n175:- `allowBundled`: optional allowlist for bundled skills only (managed/workspace skills unaffected).\n184:  clients to install private zip archives staged through `skills.upload.*`\n188:- `entries.<skillKey>.apiKey`: convenience for skills declaring a primary env var (plaintext string or SecretRef object).","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-wxlee"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779511820386}}
{"type":"message","id":"30d21a8e","parentId":"cc9d516f","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:50:29.330Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me check the correct format for skill entries in the config. The issue was \"Invalid input\" when I added `\"from\"` field. Let me look at the configuration reference for skill entries format.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ccddcb799f26481680851c0e","name":"read","arguments":{"offset":152,"path":"/app/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md","limit":80},"partialArgs":"{\"offset\": 152, \"path\": \"/app/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md\", \"limit\": 80}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779511820395,"responseId":"c61d6da25c7e44b4b7e177f131ea5807"}}
{"type":"message","id":"f2bd42c5","parentId":"30d21a8e","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:50:29.348Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ccddcb799f26481680851c0e","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"  skills: {\n    allowBundled: [\"gemini\", \"peekaboo\"],\n    load: {\n      extraDirs: [\"~/Projects/agent-scripts/skills\"],\n      allowSymlinkTargets: [\"~/Projects/manager/skills\"],\n    },\n    install: {\n      preferBrew: true,\n      nodeManager: \"npm\", // npm | pnpm | yarn | bun\n      allowUploadedArchives: false,\n    },\n    entries: {\n      \"image-lab\": {\n        apiKey: { source: \"env\", provider: \"default\", id: \"GEMINI_API_KEY\" }, // or plaintext string\n        env: { GEMINI_API_KEY: \"***\" },\n      },\n      peekaboo: { enabled: true },\n      sag: { enabled: false },\n    },\n  },\n}\n```\n\n- `allowBundled`: optional allowlist for bundled skills only (managed/workspace skills unaffected).\n- `load.extraDirs`: extra shared skill roots (lowest precedence).\n- `load.allowSymlinkTargets`: trusted real target roots that skill symlinks may\n  resolve into when the link lives outside its configured source root.\n- `install.preferBrew`: when true, prefer Homebrew installers when `brew` is\n  available before falling back to other installer kinds.\n- `install.nodeManager`: node installer preference for `metadata.openclaw.install`\n  specs (`npm` | `pnpm` | `yarn` | `bun`).\n- `install.allowUploadedArchives`: allow trusted `operator.admin` Gateway\n  clients to install private zip archives staged through `skills.upload.*`\n  (default: false). This only enables the uploaded-archive path; normal ClawHub\n  installs do not require it.\n- `entries.<skillKey>.enabled: false` disables a skill even if bundled/installed.\n- `entries.<skillKey>.apiKey`: convenience for skills declaring a primary env var (plaintext string or SecretRef object).\n\n---\n\n## Plugins\n\n```json5\n{\n  plugins: {\n    enabled: true,\n    allow: [\"voice-call\"],\n    bundledDiscovery: \"allowlist\",\n    deny: [],\n    load: {\n      paths: [\"~/Projects/oss/voice-call-plugin\"],\n    },\n    entries: {\n      \"voice-call\": {\n        enabled: true,\n        hooks: {\n          allowPromptInjection: false,\n        },\n        config: { provider: \"twilio\" },\n      },\n    },\n  },\n}\n```\n\n- Loaded from `~/.openclaw/extensions`, `<workspace>/.openclaw/extensions`, plus `plugins.load.paths`.\n- Discovery accepts native OpenClaw plugins plus compatible Codex bundles and Claude bundles, including manifestless Claude default-layout bundles.\n- **Config changes require a gateway restart.**\n- `allow`: optional allowlist (only listed plugins load). `deny` wins.\n- `bundledDiscovery`: defaults to `\"allowlist\"` for new configs, so a non-empty\n  `plugins.allow` also gates bundled provider plugins, including web-search\n  runtime providers. Doctor writes `\"compat\"` for migrated legacy allowlist\n  configs to preserve existing bundled provider behavior until you opt in.\n- `plugins.entries.<id>.apiKey`: plugin-level API key convenience field (when supported by the plugin).\n- `plugins.entries.<id>.env`: plugin-scoped env var map.\n- `plugins.entries.<id>.hooks.allowPromptInjection`: when `false`, core blocks `before_prompt_build` and ignores prompt-mutating fields from legacy `before_agent_start`, while preserving legacy `modelOverride` and `providerOverride`. Applies to native plugin hooks and supported bundle-provided hook directories.\n- `plugins.entries.<id>.hooks.allowConversationAccess`: when `true`, trusted non-bundled plugins may read raw conversation content from typed hooks such as `llm_input`, `llm_output`, `before_model_resolve`, `before_agent_reply`, `before_agent_run`, `before_agent_finalize`, and `agent_end`.\n- `plugins.entries.<id>.subagent.allowModelOverride`: explicitly trust this plugin to request per-run `provider` and `model` overrides for background subagent runs.\n- `plugins.entries.<id>.subagent.allowedModels`: optional allowlist of canonical `provider/model` targets for trusted subagent overrides. Use `\"*\"` only when you intentionally want to allow any model.\n- `plugins.entries.<id>.llm.allowModelOverride`: explicitly trust this plugin to request model overrides for `api.runtime.llm.complete`.\n\n[1163 more lines in file. Use offset=232 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779511829343}}
{"type":"message","id":"7444418c","parentId":"f2bd42c5","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:51:07.021Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The skill entry format requires `enabled: true` as a top-level property. The `from` field may not be a valid property for the config schema. Let me check the schema to understand what fields are valid for skill entries.\n\nLet me look at the existing valid skill entries to understand the correct format.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_79d72916fcfd4ba19f606c56","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw gateway config.schema.lookup skills.entries 2>&1 | head -60","timeout":10},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"openclaw gateway config.schema.lookup skills.entries 2>&1 | head -60\", \"timeout\": 10}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779511829349,"responseId":"15a9d1abe6664beda6d962bbb79df514"}}
