{"type":"message","id":"35692c5a","parentId":"57bd8c77","timestamp":"2026-05-23T05:07:46.266Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm in a conversation session that's connected to OpenClaw with the feishu channel. I should be able to use the `feishu_doc` tool directly since it's a plugin skill. Let me try using it as the agent would - just invoke the tool directly. But wait, I don't have a `feishu_doc` tool in my tool list. Let me check how the feishu tools are available to me.\n\nLooking at my available tools, I have tools like `read`, `write`, `exec`, `web_search`, etc. but not `feishu_doc`. The feishu-doc skill works through the feishu channel integration. \n\nSince I'm in a feishu direct conversation, I can use the `feishu_doc` tool that's listed in the available skills - but looking at it more carefully, feishu-doc is a \"plugin skill\" which is a tool provided to the agent at runtime. Let me check if it's actually loaded.\n\nActually, looking at the feishu-doc skill more carefully - it's listed in `~/.openclaw/plugin-skills/feishu-doc/SKILL.md`, which means it's in the plugin-skills directory but may not be enabled as a skill. The `feishu_doc` tool is part of the feishu channel integration.\n\nLet me check my tools list again... I don't see `feishu_doc` listed as a tool. So the feishu_doc tool may be a plugin that's available through the Feishu channel but not directly callable by me.\n\nWait, looking at the Gateway health output:\n```json\n\"plugins\": {\n    \"loaded\": [\n      \"duckduckgo\",\n      \"feishu\",\n      \"google\",\n      \"memory-core\",\n      \"minimax\",\n      \"nvidia\",\n      \"openclaw-weixin\",\n      \"tavily\",\n      \"volcengine\",\n      \"zai\"\n    ]\n```\n\nAnd looking at the feishu-doc SKILL.md - it says `feishu_doc` is a single tool with an action parameter. It's a feishu-provided tool that should be available through the feishu channel integration.\n\nSince I don't have the `feishu_doc` tool directly in my tool list, I should try using the `exec` tool with the gateway call approach but with the right method name. Let me try `cron.*` methods or other approaches.\n\nActually, I think the correct approach is to use the `sessions_send` or similar mechanisms. But wait - let me just try creating the doc through the feishu channel directly using the `openclaw gateway call` with the feishu_doc API.\n\nHmm, but actually I'm in this conversation. When I reply, I can use feishu_doc tool... wait, let me re-read my available tools. Looking at them, I don't have feishu_doc as a tool. \n\nActually, looking more carefully at the available skills list, I see there's `feishu-doc` in the plugin-skills directory. The feishu-doc skill mentions it's a single tool `feishu_doc`. But this tool isn't listed in my available function tools.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The feishu-doc tool is a plugin-provided tool that's available through the Feishu channel. Since I'm in a Feishu conversation, I should be able to use it. But it may need to be invoked differently - not through the standard tool interface but through the feishu channel plugin.\n\nLet me try the gateway call differently - perhaps using the proper method name.\n\nActually, I think the simplest approach is for me to try accessing it through the `cron` or other gateway endpoints. Or better yet, let me just try to use the feishu_doc tool as part of my response - if the tool is available, it should work. Let me check what tools I have available more carefully.\n\nLooking at my tool list again - no, I don't have a `feishu_doc` tool listed. These tools (like feishu-doc, feishu-wiki) might be skill tools that are available at runtime, not as predefined tools. \n\nHmm, let me try another approach. Let me see if I can invoke the feishu_doc through some API call.\n\nActually, I just realized I should look at how these feishu tools are supposed to be invoked. The skill description says it's a \"single tool `feishu_doc` with action parameter\". This suggests it's a tool that's supposed to be available to me during conversation. But it's not in my tool definitions.\n\nI think the issue is that `feishu-doc` is listed in `plugin-skills` which is for installed plugins (like feishu), and it documents how to use the `feishu_doc` tool through the feishu integration. Let me try using it directly.\n\nActually wait - let me check the feishu plugin's tools configuration.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_468c939ddbf34a4f85dba5ad","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json') as f:\n    cfg = json.load(f)\nfeishu = cfg.get('channels', {}).get('feishu', {})\nprint(json.dumps(feishu, indent=2)[:2000])\n\"","timeout":5},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nwith open('/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json') as f:\\n    cfg = json.load(f)\\nfeishu = cfg.get('channels', {}).get('feishu', {})\\nprint(json.dumps(feishu, indent=2)[:2000])\\n\\\"\", \"timeout\": 5}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779512789097,"responseId":"8fb96515389e449bafd59c905032a04f"}}
