{"type":"message","id":"a85f75cf","parentId":"3a4ebb2e","timestamp":"2026-05-23T07:25:12.972Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to test creating a Feishu document. The `feishu_doc` tool is a plugin tool that should be callable from within the agent session. Looking at the SKILL.md, it says the tool is `feishu_doc` with actions like `create`. \n\nI already successfully created a document via the API earlier (got doc_token: K4tHdGrzGoAbHIxhDhNjDocIpPb), but the permission grant failed because of missing scopes in the xiaoye app. Let me try using the feishu_doc tool properly this time - it should be available as a built-in tool in the agent context since I'm in a Feishu channel session.\n\nLet me check if the feishu_doc tool is available to me. The SKILL.md says it's a single tool `feishu_doc` with action parameter. I should be able to invoke it directly.\n\nLet me try creating a doc with the tool, using the correct owner_open_id from the inbound metadata.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e80447379d254631904d70a4","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check what tools are available to me\ngrep -r \"feishu_doc\" /home/node/.openclaw/plugin-skills/feishu-doc/ 2>/dev/null | head -5","timeout":5},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"# Check what tools are available to me\\ngrep -r \\\"feishu_doc\\\" /home/node/.openclaw/plugin-skills/feishu-doc/ 2>/dev/null | head -5\", \"timeout\": 5}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779521038605,"responseId":"6af88c8cd9d8456f8b2979cea5b19c99"}}
