{"type":"message","id":"22f79d3e","parentId":"2efc0c0d","timestamp":"2026-05-23T07:27:21.316Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to test creating a Feishu document. The `feishu_doc` tool is available as a plugin tool in OpenClaw. According to the SKILL.md, I should be able to call it directly as a tool function with parameters like `action`, `title`, `owner_open_id`.\n\nLet me try calling the tool directly in the conversation. The tool should be available as a function I can call.\n\nLooking at the SKILL.md more carefully, the tool `feishu_doc` is a skill/plugin tool. In the current agent context, tools are available. Let me try to invoke it.\n\nActually, looking at the tool schema I have available, I don't see `feishu_doc` listed as one of my tools. These are plugin-registered tools that should be available in the agent's runtime context but I don't have a direct tool binding for them in my tool list.\n\nThe SKILL.md mentions:\n- It's a plugin tool under `feishu` channel\n- The channel config has `tools.doc: true`\n- The tool is called as `feishu_doc` with action parameter\n\nSince this is a plugin tool, it should be available for me to use. Let me try calling it directly as a function.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"让我直接调用飞"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_618845beaada4489a3cb6b4f","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Read the block types reference for completeness\ncat /home/node/.openclaw/plugin-skills/feishu-doc/references/block-types.md | head -20","timeout":5},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"# Read the block types reference for completeness\\ncat /home/node/.openclaw/plugin-skills/feishu-doc/references/block-types.md | head -20\", \"timeout\": 5}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"tot